      "https://github.com/stellar/js-stellar-sdk/issues/1785"
    ],
    "notes": "canonical offer ids (int64 in XDR, 0 to 2^63-1 because core refuses negative ids from protocol 15). accepted cases carry a ManageSellOfferOp with that offer id. text is canonical only as the exact decimal rendering of an in-range value, and refused with a sign (including -0), whitespace, a radix prefix, an exponent, non-ASCII digits, when empty or out of range; a JSON number is canonical as an integer in range with |n| <= 2^53-1, and refused when negative, non-integral or out of range. leading-zero text, integral numbers written with .0 and in-range numbers above 2^53-1 are in a separate implementation-defined entry. negative offer ids are refused because core answers MANAGE_SELL_OFFER_MALFORMED / MANAGE_BUY_OFFER_MALFORMED for offerID < 0 from protocol 15 (stellar-core v30.0.0 src/transactions/ManageOfferOpFrameBase.cpp, ManageOfferOpFrameBase::doCheckValid). the reject reason is informational; a testee passes by refusing.",
    "passphrase_dependent": false,
